A: You need to add str in your format, so it will work.
def zipcode(month, lr):
  return {month.count('z'), for i in range(3)}
print zipcode(5)

If you want to generate an array with all months that start with g, then use this:
$months = [];
$year = 0;
while ($month = date("F", mktime($year, 0, 0, 1, 1))) {
    $months[] = $month;
}

echo count($months);
print_r($months);

This would give you an array with 26 items, with month name in English (golf, .., zulu), see it working here.

Lettersq = {
    q:
    monthsInYear | 1..12 | (
        isLetter(m) and hasEnd(m,"q")
    )
}

The first output the number of times a month starts with q. The second output the values that are months and starts with q.
Since the first argument to the filter is a variable, this is a slow lookup, and will only work for short lists.
